From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: bpereira <bpereira@cloudflare.com>
Date: Tue, 4 Aug 2026 14:38:22 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] Skip painting a subtree behind an empty clip region

An empty clip region discards every pixel below it, but the painter
still pushed the layer and rasterized the whole subtree into it before
the clip threw the result away. On 1400 stacked visually-hidden spans
(the `clip: rect(0,0,0,0)` plus `clip-path: inset(50%)` idiom) at
1280x900 that cost 40.6 ms/frame against a 14.1 ms visibility:hidden
floor: 87% of the price of painting the text, for zero visible pixels.

Skipping is pixel-identical: everything below the early-out paints
inside the layer whose region is empty, so it contributes nothing
anyway. Descendants that leave the box are covered too. A re-homed
abspos still paints from its flow parent, so it is inside the layer and
already invisible, and a position:fixed box is hoisted to be a layout
child of the root with no paint_parent_override, so it never entered
this subtree. Hit testing walks paint_children separately, so it is
untouched.

One difference: past LAYER_LIMIT a refused clip painted its content
unclipped and visible, and now it stays hidden. That is what an empty
region means, and it only matters 1024 open layers deep, where the
page is already mis-rendering everything else.

Upstream already returns early for an empty `clip: rect()`, so this
only adds the clip-path half. Outline and outset box shadow paint
outside the clip-path layer here, so they stay above the early-out.
Clipping them away would be the spec behaviour, but that is a separate
change, not part of an optimisation.
---
 src/render.rs | 32 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++----
 1 file changed, 28 insertions(+), 4 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/render.rs b/src/render.rs
index 5e77751..890e806 100644
--- a/src/render.rs
+++ b/src/render.rs
@@ -40,7 +40,7 @@ use style::{
     },
 };

-use kurbo::{self, Affine, Insets, Point, Rect, Shape, Size, Stroke, Vec2};
+use kurbo::{self, Affine, BezPath, Insets, Point, Rect, Shape, Size, Stroke, Vec2};
 use peniko::{self, Fill, ImageData, ImageSampler};
 use style::values::generics::color::GenericColor;
 use taffy::Layout;
@@ -481,9 +481,6 @@ impl<'dom, 'a> BlitzDomPainter<'dom, 'a> {
         // Compute clip-path (if any) and wrap all rendering in a clip layer
         let clip_path_shape = cx.clip_path_shape();
         let has_clip_path = clip_path_shape.is_some();
-        let default_clip = cx.frame.border_box_path();
-        let mut clip_path_for_layer = clip_path_shape.unwrap_or(default_clip);
-        clip_path_for_layer.apply_affine(Affine::scale(self.scale));

         // CSS 2 `clip` property (absolutely positioned elements only). Applies to the whole of
         // the element's rendering (including outlines and shadows), so it is the outermost layer.
@@ -501,9 +498,25 @@ impl<'dom, 'a> BlitzDomPainter<'dom, 'a> {
             None,
         );

+        // An empty clip-path region means every pixel the subtree paints is discarded
+        // by the layer that wraps it, so the whole traversal below is dead work.
+        let clipped_away = is_empty_clip_region(clip_path_shape.as_ref());
+
         cx.draw_outline(scene);
         cx.draw_outset_box_shadow(scene);

+        // Outline and outset shadow paint outside the clip-path layer here, so they
+        // stay above the skip to keep an empty-clipped frame pixel-identical.
+        if clipped_away {
+            self.layer_manager
+                .maybe_pop_layer(scene, css_clip_layer_pushed);
+            return;
+        }
+
+        let default_clip = cx.frame.border_box_path();
+        let mut clip_path_for_layer = clip_path_shape.unwrap_or(default_clip);
+        clip_path_for_layer.apply_affine(Affine::scale(self.scale));
+
         // clip-path clip ayer
         self.layer_manager.maybe_with_layer(
             scene,
@@ -766,6 +779,17 @@ fn convert_rect(rect: &parley::BoundingBox) -> kurbo::Rect {
     peniko::kurbo::Rect::new(rect.x0, rect.y0, rect.x1, rect.y1)
 }

+/// Whether a resolved clip region covers no area, and so hides the element and
+/// everything painted inside its clip layer.
+fn is_empty_clip_region(shape: Option<&BezPath>) -> bool {
+    // Zero-area bounding box is sufficient, not necessary: it catches the empty
+    // rects inset() collapses to without walking odd-even fill rules.
+    shape.is_some_and(|shape| {
+        let bounds = shape.bounding_box();
+        bounds.width() <= 0.0 || bounds.height() <= 0.0
+    })
+}
+
 impl ElementCx<'_, '_> {
     /// Paint overlay scrollbar thumbs for scroll containers: `overflow:
     /// scroll`, or `auto` when the content overflows (never `hidden`/`clip`,
